<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AY8-QA-005/ay8-3>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "crates/atm-herdr/tests/socket_construction_pin.rs" ;
  triage:line 130 ;
  triage:snippet "let is_integration_test = source.starts_with(manifest.join(\"tests\")); if is_integration_test { continue; }" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:branch "feature/ay8-herdr-socket-transport" ;
  triage:headSha "26ea2806a" ;
  triage:occursIn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/ay8-26ea2806a> ;
  triage:note "quality-mgr qa-pr1280-r3: sub-issues (1) type-alias construction and (2) fn-pointer-style construction are now genuinely fixed — socket_construction_pin.rs replaces the substring match with a real syn::visit::Visit-based SocketConstructorVisitor that resolves use-aliases and syn::Item::Type aliases of HerdrIo, and a collect_aliases/cfg_test_attribute pass replaces the old first-cfg(test)-only logic, closing sub-issue (3) as well. Sub-issue (4) is NOT fixed: socket_variant_constructed_only_in_tests (lines 117-140) collects sources from both src/ and tests/, but then unconditionally `continue`s past every file under tests/ before running construction_findings on it, so the tests/ half of the allowlist is still never actually scanned — the exact literal defect originally reported. Additionally, the fix for sub-issues 1-3 added crates/atm-herdr/Cargo.toml dev-dependency syn.workspace=true without updating boundaries/atm-herdr/herdr-process-adapter.toml's allowed_dependencies, causing a new live blocking CI regression — see AY8-QA-007. Finding stays open (important); 3 of 4 sub-issues genuinely fixed, 1 remains and 1 side-effect regression introduced." .

