<urn:atm:triage:resolution/AY8-QA-005/1>
  a triage:Resolution ;
  triage:resolvedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:resolvedAt "2026-09-07T07:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:fixCommit "690f86ea583f80b975e5ef019c77bb1befacd33e" ;
  triage:fixBranch "feature/ay8-herdr-socket-transport" ;
  triage:verifiedInRound "qa-pr1280-r4" ;
  triage:resolutionNote "Out of this round's assigned fix scope, but independently verified fully resolved as an incidental side effect of the AY8-QA-007 syn-removal rewrite, so closing on direct evidence rather than leaving ambiguous. Sub-issues (1)-(3) were already fixed in r3 and remain intact under the new dependency-free lexer (construction_pin_detects_aliases_and_variant_function_pointers explicitly re-proves alias and function-pointer-form detection plus comment/string-literal false-positive avoidance). Sub-issue (4), the literal originally-reported defect ('tests/ half of the allowlist is never actually scanned'), is now fixed: read socket_variant_constructed_only_in_tests (lines 152-184) directly -- `lex_rust(&contents)` and `construction_findings` now run unconditionally on every source including everything under tests/, with `is_integration_test` files given a full-file allowed range (`vec![(0, contents.len())]`) rather than being `continue`d past unprocessed. This both scans tests/ (fixing the literal complaint) and matches D10's own stated intent that HerdrIo::Socket construction is permitted throughout crates/atm-herdr/tests/. Verified locally: `cargo test -p atm-herdr --all-features` -- all 3 socket_construction_pin tests pass, including socket_variant_constructed_only_in_tests. All 3 occurrences closed." .